@startuml
title SmartPark - View Parking Availability
autonumber

actor Student
participant "React frontend\n(App / useParkingAvailability)" as React
participant "Flask API\nGET /api/decks" as Flask
participant "SQLAlchemy ORM\n(SessionLocal)" as ORM
database "SQLite\n(DATABASE_PATH)" as DB

Student -> React: Open parking availability
activate React
React -> Flask: GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/decks
note over React,Flask
  Browser request from Vite's http://127.0.0.1:5173 origin;
  Flask CORS allows this origin.
end note
activate Flask
Flask -> ORM: Open SessionLocal; select ParkingDeck\nordered by id
activate ORM
ORM -> DB: SELECT mapped parking_decks columns\nFROM parking_decks ORDER BY id
activate DB
DB --> ORM: Ordered persisted deck rows
deactivate DB
ORM --> Flask: ParkingDeck objects
deactivate ORM
Flask -> Flask: Map columns to JSON keys;\nset occupiedSpaces to null if data unavailable
Flask --> React: 200 JSON array of decks
deactivate Flask
React -> React: Map API JSON to UI deck shape;\nset decks and lastRefresh
React --> Student: Render deck cards, availability,\nand update time
deactivate React

note over React
  The hook fetches the API once on mount.
  Its existing 30-second timer simulates occupancy
  changes locally; it does not re-fetch SQLite data.
  Database rows are initialized/upserted from demo CSVs,
  not supplied by a live sensor feed.
end note
@enduml
